    file_write_bytes_truncates_to_3_bytes_under_codegen_2026-08-27, 0, "Registration of unresolved tracking document. Priority: untriaged; P3 is a registration placeholder. The document remains the authority for diagnosis, ownership, and acceptance; this row does not claim implementation or closure."
    file_write_bytes_truncates_to_3_bytes_under_codegen_2026-08-27, 1015, "2026-11-05 rel100-armfix: NOT FIXED root cause is seed extern [u8] argument marshalling on compiled call sites in src/compiler_rust, outside the stdlib lane's authority; interpreted facade contract pinned for any future marshalling fix (evidence: test/01_unit/lib/io/file_write_bytes_roundtrip_spec.spl 3/3 interpreted on seed release100-7a0e6fe516f-20261031)"
    file_write_bytes_truncates_to_3_bytes_under_codegen_2026-08-27, 1018, "2026-11-05 rel100-r2: FIXED-in-source verified — extern [u8] marshalling defect already repaired at release/1.0.0 by the rt_file_write_bytes -> rt_file_write_bytes_array owner-preserving alias (Cranelift sffi_alias_target calls.rs:3737, LLVM map_sffi_name) plus import-linkage non-shadowing (calls.rs:3830-3842); round-1 host failures were an older-binary artifact. New JIT regression test pins the 2-owner-word ABI and full 256-byte high-bit-set payload (cargo test file_write_bytes 1/1, calls 30/30); compiled end-to-end write verified on a worktree-built seed (5/5 and 256/256 bytes, no engine demotion); interpreted contract spec 3/3. Remaining suspect only if regressed: pure-Simple self-hosted compiler path."

